## **Psalm 101: The Ethics of Integrity and Right Association**

### **Introduction**

Psalm 101 is a psalm of royal commitment and ethical resolve, attributed to David. It is a declaration of the king's intention to rule with integrity, justice, and righteousness. The psalmist promises to sing of steadfast love and justice, to walk with integrity of heart, and to set no evil thing before their eyes. The psalm outlines the king's commitment to surround themselves with the faithful, to banish the wicked, and to uphold righteousness in the land.

### **Full Biblical Text**

****Of David. A Psalm.****

****1**** I will sing of steadfast love and justice; to you, O LORD, I will sing praises. ****2**** I will study the way that is blameless. When shall I attain it? I will walk with integrity of heart within my house; ****3**** I will not set before my eyes anything that is base. I hate the work of those who fall away; it shall not cling to me. ****4**** Perverseness of heart shall be far from me; I will know nothing of evil. ****5**** One who secretly slanders a neighbor I will destroy. A haughty look and an arrogant heart I will not tolerate. ****6**** I will look with favor on the faithful in the land, so that they may live with me; those who walk in the way of integrity shall minister to me. ****7**** No one who practices deceit shall remain in my house; no one who utters lies shall continue in my presence. ****8**** Morning by morning I will destroy all the wicked in the land, cutting off all evildoers from the city of the LORD.

